/**
 * roller-coasters.js — 157 US roller coasters, the plugin's sample dataset.
 *
 * Copied from codap-spirit-animal `web/src/demo/coasters.js`. It is the sample
 * here because the exploration model was fitted to logs of a CODAP activity
 * titled "Roller Coasters". That this is the same data the activity used is
 * an assumption (the log extract does not carry the dataset), not a check.
 *
 * PROVENANCE: transcribed 2026-09-08 from CODAP's own example document,
 * `example-documents/src/documents/rollercoasters.codap` in
 * github.com/concord-consortium/codap-data. Values are unmodified; only the
 * parent `States` collection and its boundary polygons were dropped, because
 * nothing in the wonderings pipeline reads geography.
 *
 * WHY THIS AND NOT MAMMALS. Mammals has 12 cases, and at n=12 the significance
 * floor is |r| >= 0.576 — so 2 of 10 numeric pairs qualified and the panel had
 * almost nothing to say. Here n is ~145 per pair, the floor is ~0.16, and 16 of
 * 36 pairs qualify. Measured 2026-09-08: an empty workspace earns 39 wonderings
 * against Mammals' 16.
 *
 * It also carries UNITS (mph, ft, sec) and REAL MISSING DATA — `Duration` is
 * blank on a dozen coasters, which is what exercises the pairwise-complete
 * correlation fix on something other than a synthetic fixture.
 *
 * Kept deliberately: `latitude`/`longitude` (they are why the geographic role
 * exists) and the derived pairs `Age_Group`/`Year_Opened` and
 * `Inversions`/`Num_of_Inversions` (they are why derived-column detection
 * exists). Removing them would delete the test cases.
 */
